DEVELOPMENT

To set up and run the project locally, the following prerequisites are needed: Node.js version 18 or higher and npm.

The available commands are:
"npm install" to install all project dependencies.
"npm run dev" to start the Vite development server with hot module replacement.
"npm run build" to create a production build in the /dist directory.
"npm run preview" to preview the production build locally.
"npm run lint" to run ESLint across the project.


DEPLOYMENT

The website is built as static assets using Vite and deployed to Vercel. The production build output is generated in the /dist directory. Each of the three featured project demos is also hosted on Vercel under separate subdomains.


SEARCH ENGINE OPTIMIZATION

The website is optimized for search engines with the following measures: Open Graph meta tags for social media sharing, Twitter Card meta tags, semantic HTML structure throughout all pages, dynamic page titles that update per route, and meta descriptions included in the index.html file.


